Add a command line option to load a save at start-up

`--dev-load-game=N` loads the save in slot N (1-10) as soon as the engine
is up, instead of stopping at the main menu. Fallout 2 CE has the same
option under the same name. If the slot cannot be loaded the game says so
and goes to the main menu as usual.

The slot is loaded the way a quick load loads it once its slot is known,
so no part of the load screen is shown.
---
diff --git a/src/game/loadsave.cc b/src/game/loadsave.cc
index 119487e..711d442 100644
--- a/src/game/loadsave.cc
+++ b/src/game/loadsave.cc
@@ -1245,6 +1245,26 @@ int LoadGame(int mode)
     return rc;
 }
 
+// CE: Loads the save in the given slot (zero-based) without asking, the way a
+// quick load does once its slot has been picked.
+int LoadGameInSlot(int slot)
+{
+    if (slot < 0 || slot > 9) {
+        return -1;
+    }
+
+    slot_cursor = slot;
+    quick_done = true;
+
+    int rc = LoadGame(LOAD_SAVE_MODE_QUICK);
+
+    // As after loading from the main menu: the first quick save asks for
+    // its slot instead of silently reusing this one.
+    quick_done = false;
+
+    return rc;
+}
